                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hmmm. \n\n   I would actually opine that the visual \"style\" of this product is quite good. No, not the crap-arsed promo pic with the garish red writing that looks like a three-year-old just discovered their first crayon...but the twisted photographic style in the game itself (resourcefully used as an alternative to finding an actual artist, one presumes). Regrettably, this is still a text-based adventure, and while the writing's vaguely passable...the story certainly isn't.\n\n   You know you're in trouble when one of your first decisions as a player is to use the elevator or the stairs, and choosing the former just gets you insta-killed with no warning whatsoever. It would be a tad hysterical to call this game \"bad\"...but, y'know, I'm not gonna go outta my way to call it \"good\", either. And that five-dollar price tag really is rather silly...\n\n   If you're gonna bother, you REALLY should wait for a sale.\n\nVerdict: 4/10.",
